// {"files":[{"path":"\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\danie\\OneDrive\\github-repos\\ai-chat-webui\\supabase\\README.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":68,"oldLines":7,"newStart":68,"newLines":36,"lines":[" docker compose --env-file supabase/.env -f supabase/docker-compose.yml up -d auth rest gateway"," ```"," ","-## 5. Production notes","+## 5. Reverse proxy (production)","+","+Expose only two HTTPS endpoints: the app and the gateway's public URL.","+Database, Auth-direct, and PostgREST-direct ports stay bound to localhost.","+Example Caddy configuration on the same host:","+","+```caddy","+app.example.com {","+    reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:3000","+}","+","+api.example.com {","+    reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8000","+}","+```","+","+Set `SUPABASE_PUBLIC_URL=https://api.example.com`,","+`API_EXTERNAL_URL=https://api.example.com/auth/v1`, and","+`SITE_URL=https://app.example.com` in `supabase/.env`, and add the public","+app URL to the app's `ALLOWED_ORIGIN`/`APP_PUBLIC_URL` (see root","+`.env.example`). Apply rate limiting at this layer.","+","+## 6. Removing a login (account deletion)","+","+\"Delete all my data\" in Settings removes every row the user owns. The","+Supabase Auth user itself is removed by the operator in Studio","+(Authentication → Users → Delete user) or via the Auth admin API with the","+service-role key — that key is never placed in app code or the app `.env`.","+","+## 7. Production notes"," "," - Keep all component ports bound to localhost and terminate TLS in a reverse","   proxy. Expose only the app and the gateway's public URL."]}]}]}
